    "turn": {
     "status": "completed",
     "text": "{\"root_cause\": \"The agent treated PaymentTimeout as a definite failure and retried issue_refund with a fresh idempotency key (auto-2) without re-reading state. However timeout_after_commit means the first refund (auto-1) had already committed, so the retry created a second distinct 250000 refund, totaling 500000 and duplicating the full refund.\", \"proposed_patch\": \"On PaymentTimeout/ambiguous timeout from issue_refund, never generate a new key: first call get_order/list_refunds to check if the amount already committed, and if retrying, reuse the original key verbatim. Pseudo-code: except PaymentTimeout: if get_order(...).refunded_minor >= amount_minor: return existing_refund; else retry issue_refund(amount_minor, customer_id, order_id, idempotency_key=original_key) with bounded retries.\"}",
